  "caption": "Quinn's arm started buzzing with pins and needles, the neck joined in, and the internet made it sound like doom.\n\nNeck pain with pain, tingling, numbness or weakness down the arm is often an irritated nerve root. Many people improve with time and active rehab, and a scan isn't automatically needed to get started. Understanding it can ease the worry.\n\nWhat often helps: finding positions that ease the arm, gentle neck movement, shoulder-blade control and gradual arm strengthening, progressed to suit you, not copied from random videos.\n\nGet assessed promptly for worsening weakness, clumsiness, balance changes, symptoms in both arms or legs, bladder or bowel changes or fever. Sudden face or speech changes or a severe unusual headache: call 000.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
